    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20331" root="سلب" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَلَبَةٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَلَبٌ</span>, in the former half of the paragraph: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سِلَابٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A string,</i>
or <i>cord, that is tied to the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَطْم</span> [i. e. <i>muzzle,</i> or
<i>nose,</i>] <i>of the camel, exclusive of the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِطَام</span> [q. v.].
(M.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>A sinew that is bound upon an
arrow:</i> accord. to AHn, the <i>sinew that is wound
upon the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِيط</span> [or <i>skin of the reed,</i> or <i>cane,</i>] <i>of the
arrow.</i> (M.)

